course: dictionary
lesson: 7893
title: Rant: angry, long and loud
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rant is talking or shouting for a long time in an angry way, often without listening to anyone else. Rant can be a verb (to rant) or a noun (a rant). Context helps: «Dad had a rant about the broken washing machine.» Dad is cross and keeps going on and on, so a rant is an angry, long complaint.
explain: Look for clues in the words around it. «The coach ranted at the referee for ten minutes.» Ten minutes is a long time, and the coach is angry at the referee. Test your meaning by swapping it in: "The coach complained angrily for ten minutes" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Online, a rant is a long complaining post or video. «Her rant about homework was posted for everyone to see.» Phrases such as go on a rant and have a rant tell you the same thing: someone is letting their anger out in words.
fact: Rant can be a verb (to rant) or a noun (a rant).
fact: «Rant» means to talk or shout for a long time in an angry, excited way.
fact: Online, a rant is a post or video where someone complains loudly about something.
fact: «A tantrum with a keyboard» means an angry online rant.
fact: Common phrases: rant about, rant and rave, go on a rant, have a rant.
exercise: «Dad had a rant about the broken washing machine.» What does rant mean here? | *A long, angry complaint | A quiet, happy song | A short hug | A new washing powder
exercise: «The coach ranted at the referee for ten minutes.» Which words are a clue that the rant was long? | ranted | *for ten minutes | The coach | at the referee
exercise: Ella reads «a tantrum with a keyboard» and says it means a happy game. What does it really mean? | *An angry online rant | A piano lesson | A quiet time with a computer | A happy game played on a keyboard
test: «After the match, Sam went on a rant about the unfair referee.» What does go on a rant mean? | Sing loudly with friends | Go for a long run | Stop talking and sit down | *Talk angrily for a long time
test: «Her rant about homework was posted online for everyone to see.» What is an online rant? | A short, silent video | *A post or video where someone complains loudly | A drawing of a cat | A game with lots of levels
exam: «Her rant lasted ten minutes.» What part of speech is rant in this sentence? | Adjective | Adverb | *Noun | Verb
